Discovered — the cause of the crash was that my script was stat-ing `new` *after* the staging rename (the path had already been moved). But an actual design fact came to light: the staged copy's mtime was the copy timestamp, not the source's mtime — `copy_file` does not preserve mtime, so the published manifest needs to retain the source-space state. Re-running C–I correctly:
